**How to implement.** Kit files changed outside the app are offered for reload, with Reload and Keep mine (001 §E 'on activation, files changed outside the app (another editor, git, a sync) are offered for reload'; 001 §O 'Kit menu: … Reload changes'; the S5.3 brief: on window activation run S4.1's external-change check; changed files are listed with Reload (re-read them into the model) and Keep mine; Reload changes in the Kit menu runs the same check on demand; step 130: `changedKitFiles` answers the kit files whose stamp differs from the recorded one, and never the proxy's own writes). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: (1) Before the model: `KitCheckOrigin` = `KitCheckOnActivation` (the window was activated) | `KitCheckOnRequest` (the Kit menu's Reload changes). (2) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `kitChanges : FileName list` after `kitShell` (step 186), documented in one line: the kit files changed outside the app that the kit bar offers to reload, in `changedKitFiles`' order, empty when nothing is offered; `initWith` sets it to `[]`. (3) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `CheckKitChanges of KitCheckOrigin`, `ReloadKitChanges` (the offer's Reload) and `KeepMyKitChanges` (the offer's Keep mine). (4) What `loadKit` sets from a kit's content (`kit`, `experimentCollection` through `ExperimentCollection.ofLoaded` (`Experiments.fs:324`), `savedScenes` (step 153) and `experimentDataStatus` through the one private validation function, steps 152 and 184) moves into one private function of the kit context, its experiments and its scene names, which `loadKit` calls with `opened`'s, so a reload sets exactly what an open sets; `loadKit` keeps setting `experimentData` and `kitFolderOpt` itself. (5) Arms. A model whose `kitFolderOpt` is `None` answers all three unchanged, because nothing outside the app can change a scratch kit. `CheckKitChanges origin` calls `model.kit.proxy.changedKitFiles ()` (step 130): `Ok []` sets `kitChanges` to `[]` and, for `KitCheckOnRequest` only, `kitStatus` to `No kit file changed outside the app.`; `Ok files` sets `kitChanges` to `files` and changes nothing else, so an open offer is replaced by the current list; `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `The kit could not be checked for changes — <e.describe>`. `ReloadKitChanges` reads `model.kit.proxy.readKitFile ()` (step 125), `readExperiments ()` and `readSceneNames ()` (step 148), then calls `recordStamps ()` (step 130); when all answer `Ok`, the model holds the re-read kit file in `kit` (its proxy, `access` and `clock` kept) and the re-read experiments and scene names through (4), the draft starting fresh as an open's does, `kitChanges` is `[]` and `kitStatus` is `None`; the first `Error e` keeps the model and its offer and sets `kitStatus` to `The kit could not be reloaded — <e.describe>`. `KeepMyKitChanges` calls `recordStamps ()`: `Ok ()` sets `kitChanges` to `[]`, so the same changes are not offered again and the window's next write of such a file replaces it; `Error e` keeps the offer and sets the check's status text. None of the three writes a kit file, so a read-only kit is offered reloads too (step 131: `recordStamps` and `changedKitFiles` pass through `readOnlyView`). No merge, per-file choice, diff, file watcher or timer is added: the check runs when the window is activated (step 189) and on request (step 188). Tests, in `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184). Another writer is `KitProxy.create` over the kit's folder (step 126), which takes no lock, writing through `writeExperiment` (step 148) and `writeKitFile` (step 125); its experiment `E2` is the committed experiment with `id = ExperimentId 2`. `files another writer changed are offered, and the window's own writes are not`: after `ExpCommit` of an experiment through the model, `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnActivation` offers nothing; after the other writer writes `E2` and the kit file named `Renamed`, it offers exactly `.kit-json` and `E2.experiment-json`. `Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer`: `ReloadKitChanges` then leaves the model holding `E2`, the kit named `Renamed` (its title starting `Renamed`) and no offer, and a second check offers nothing. `Keep mine keeps the model and clears the offer until the next change`: `KeepMyKitChanges` instead leaves the experiments and the kit's name as they were and no offer; a second check offers nothing; and a further write of the other writer is offered again. `a requested check with nothing changed says so, and an activation check stays silent`: over an unchanged kit, `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnRequest` sets `kitStatus` to `No kit file changed outside the app.`, and `KitCheckOnActivation` leaves `kitStatus` `None`. `a kit opened read-only is offered changes and reloads them`: over the kit opened read-only, the other writer's `E2` is offered and `ReloadKitChanges` reads it in, and the window's proxy writes no file. `InverseConstructorTests`' and `SceneSaveLoadTests`' facts that load a kit through `loadKit` (steps 152, 153) keep their assertions over the moved body.

**Acceptance.** After reload lands, `CheckKitChanges` MUST offer exactly the kit files another writer changed, `ReloadKitChanges` MUST re-read the kit file, experiments and scenes into the model and clear the offer, and `KeepMyKitChanges` MUST clear the offer keeping the model; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `files another writer changed are offered, and the window's own writes are not`, `Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer`, `Keep mine keeps the model and clears the offer until the next change`, `a requested check with nothing changed says so, and an activation check stays silent` and `a kit opened read-only is offered changes and reloads them`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.
